Status: DONE
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/BowserBoy/issues/110
Milestone: Move the axolotl around the desk like pear-boy.
Dependencies: 110_SMALL_AXOLOTL_LAMP.todo; existing DeskMotion and desk clearance.
Purpose: Give the smaller companion the same real pointer/touch dragging,
depth adjustment, keyboard placement and gravity while preserving lighting.

Tasks:
- [x] Reuse DeskMotion and shared companion gesture handling.
- [x] Preserve short-click power; dragging never toggles the glow.
- [x] Add keyboard Move and Reset controls, cancellation and desk bounds.
- [x] Integrate moving bounds into console collision, clearance and focus poses.
- [x] Qualify desktop rendered fall/bounce and phone touch/keyboard regression.
- [x] Update affected documentation, tracking and owned continuity.

Acceptance criteria:
Actual desktop and touch gestures move the axolotl in 3D without moving
pear-boy or opening console tools. Wheel adjusts depth. Release/Enter shows
the falling and bouncing model before settling; no below-table penetration.
Escape, pointer cancellation, blur and resize restore pickup position.
Lighting stays independent and follows the body; a click still toggles.
The original tripod and companion block overlap; table consoles yield.
Focused GBA/DS transitions can clear the body without losing its table pose.
No new face/rope animation, persistence or emulator changes.

Completion evidence:
Desktop actual drag/depth/rendered fall+bounce/cancel/yield and phone real
touch/keyboard/resize cases pass, alongside retained Pear light/movement.
The preceding gate passes six other UI/lighting/shimmer cases;61units,
syntax and build pass. An independent real-browser check moves the lamp
through GBA/DS Play/Inspect/table, verifies six clear poses and restores
its selected table coordinates. Companion rejection, blur cancellation,
occupied Pear home error, both lamp resets and console reset also pass;
no page errors. Publication belongs to112, not this local completion.

Completion log:
2026-11-07: Owner explicitly requests movement after the fixed lamp in110.
Supersede that fixed-position constraint, not its original completion evidence.
Extract common companion gesture handling instead of copying pear movement;
use actual rotated body bounds with existing fixed-step DeskMotion.
2026-11-07: First tests expose a Vector3/Object3D helper error and actual
console reset seeds predating lamp clearance. Fix projection and save the
first collision-free console homes; all three repaired cases pass.
Prevent Pear reset from overlapping the moved axolotl, with explicit
operation error reporting. Separate console wheel-only fixture fails,
one attempted fixture repair is rejected, and that exact CI case is parked
under105 per owner instruction. Its coverage is not claimed restored.
